{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Titan Consolidated — Spread Five Years, Build the Spine",
  "scenario": "You're joining Bajaj Finance's equity desk on Monday. Your first task: build the foundation of a Titan Company model — load five years of audited consolidated statements, set up the date spine and A/E flag row that every tab will share, and tie out the history to the annual report. The model won't forecast anything yet; it will hold real truth, organised professionally.",
  "instructions": "Spread Titan's consolidated P&L and balance-sheet figures into the Historicals sheet, complete the date spine using EOMONTH, add the A/E flag row, and perform tie-out checks against the filing. Your model architecture separates Inputs (assumptions) from Engine (formulas) from Outputs — this exercise builds the Engine's foundation with real data.",
  "learning_objective": "Construct a professional three-layer model spine with a date-driven actual-versus-estimate flag row, load five years of real consolidated historical data with balance checks, and tie out key totals to verify the spread against the annual report.",
  "hints": [
    "The anchor date in cell B2 is 31-Mar-2025 (the latest actual year-end). Column C is FY21; column G is FY25. Use EOMONTH(previous_cell, 12) to derive each date, then custom-format as 'FY'YY.",
    "The A/E flag row uses =IF(C$4<=$B$2,\"A\",\"E\") filled across — it compares each column's date to the anchor and returns 'A' for actual (history), 'E' for estimate (forecast).",
    "Balance-check: Total Assets (row 24) must equal Total Equity & Liabilities (row 34) for each year. Write =ROUND(C24-C34,1) in the check row — it must read 0.0 for every column. Tied-out totals: Revenue (row 2), EBITDA (row 8), PAT (row 13), Total Assets (row 24)."
  ],
